.SS "\fBCompareResult\fP SystemEx\&.Algorithms\&.ValueComparer< T >\&.Compare (Optional< T > x, Optional< T > y)"

.PP
Compares two numeric values using relational operators provided by INumber<T>\&. Supports both strict and non‑strict ordering\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIx\fP The first numeric value\&. May be \fRnull\fP\&.
.br
\fIy\fP The second numeric value\&. May be \fRnull\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A \fBCompareResult\fP describing the relation: 
.PD 0
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBCompareResult\&.EqualLess\fP if \fRx <= y\fP\&. 
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBCompareResult\&.EqualGreater\fP if \fRx >= y\fP\&. 
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBCompareResult\&.Less\fP if \fRx < y\fP\&. 
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBCompareResult\&.Greater\fP if \fRx > y\fP\&. 
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBCompareResult\&.Equal\fP if both values are numerically equal\&. 
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBCompareResult\&.Null\fP if both values are \fRnull\fP\&. 
.PP
.RE
